# This repository is written on Windows, but it will be cloned on Linux and macOS too. Without
# this rule git stores the local CRLFs, and the first collaborator on another system sees EVERY
# file as modified in full — a diff nobody can read, over a change that does not exist.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` normalises to LF in the repository and leaves the local checkout alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries: never touched.
*.png binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ico binary
*.jpg binary
*.aab binary
*.apk binary
*.keystore binary
*.jks binary

# Capacitor/Gradle, once android/ exists. gradle-wrapper.jar is binary and `text=auto` usually
# guesses that right — but "usually" is not a guarantee for a file that, once corrupted, makes
# the build fail with an error about missing classes. gradlew.bat has to stay CRLF: cmd.exe
# runs it line by line and a .bat with LF behaves unpredictably.
*.jar binary
*.bat text eol=crlf
